icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.6229 9.64789C13.8798 9.54672 14.1701 9.6724 14.2714 9.92914L15.2792 12.4878C16.0889 14.5432 15.0788 16.8666 13.0233 17.6763C11.0323 18.4603 8.79012 17.5367 7.91585 15.6098L7.83577 15.4204L6.82795 12.8618C6.72674 12.6048 6.85325 12.3145 7.11018 12.2133C7.36701 12.1122 7.65732 12.2379 7.75862 12.4946L8.76645 15.0532C9.37368 16.5947 11.1156 17.3528 12.6571 16.7456C14.1986 16.1384 14.9557 14.3965 14.3485 12.8549L13.3407 10.2963C13.2395 10.0395 13.3661 9.74917 13.6229 9.64789ZM8.90024 7.20842C9.15717 7.10721 9.44747 7.23372 9.54868 7.49065L11.3817 12.143C11.4826 12.3998 11.3563 12.6903 11.0995 12.7915C10.8426 12.8925 10.5523 12.766 10.451 12.5092L8.61898 7.85686C8.5178 7.59999 8.64342 7.30969 8.90024 7.20842ZM7.16975 2.25331C9.17539 1.57852 11.3796 2.58838 12.1639 4.5795L13.1718 7.13811C13.273 7.39504 13.1465 7.68534 12.8895 7.78655C12.6327 7.88749 12.3423 7.76113 12.2411 7.50432L11.2333 4.94571C10.6259 3.40439 8.88406 2.6471 7.3426 3.25429C5.80118 3.86161 5.04399 5.60345 5.65118 7.14494L6.659 9.70355C6.76021 9.96048 6.6337 10.2508 6.37677 10.352C6.11988 10.4531 5.82952 10.3266 5.72833 10.0698L4.7205 7.51116C3.91111 5.45581 4.92107 3.13323 6.97639 2.32362L7.16975 2.25331Z" /></svg></span>Blog</span></span></a></div><div class="ResourceList-module-scss-module__RXHz9G__item" style="--reveal-index:3"><a href="https://red.anthropic.com/2026/critical-infrastructure-defense/" class="CardLink-module-scss-module__E6qfaW__card ResourceList-module-scss-module__RXHz9G__gridCard" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><p class="CardLink-module-scss-module__E6qfaW__title text-body-2-serif">Experimenting with AI to defend critical infrastructure</p><span class="CardLink-module-scss-module__E6qfaW__bottom"><span class="CardLink-module-scss-module__E6qfaW__linkLabel text-caption"><span class="CardLink-module-scss-module__E6qfaW__icon"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M13.6229 9.64789C13.8798 9.54672 14.1701 9.6724 14.2714 9.92914L15.2792 12.4878C16.0889 14.5432 15.0788 16.8666 13.0233 17.6763C11.0323 18.4603 8.79012 17.5367 7.91585 15.6098L7.83577 15.4204L6.82795 12.8618C6.72674 12.6048 6.85325 12.3145 7.11018 12.2133C7.36701 12.1122 7.65732 12.2379 7.75862 12.4946L8.76645 15.0532C9.37368 16.5947 11.1156 17.3528 12.6571 16.7456C14.1986 16.1384 14.9557 14.3965 14.3485 12.8549L13.3407 10.2963C13.2395 10.0395 13.3661 9.74917 13.6229 9.64789ZM8.90024 7.20842C9.15717 7.10721 9.44747 7.23372 9.54868 7.49065L11.3817 12.143C11.4826 12.3998 11.3563 12.6903 11.0995 12.7915C10.8426 12.8925 10.5523 12.766 10.451 12.5092L8.61898 7.85686C8.5178 7.59999 8.64342 7.30969 8.90024 7.20842ZM7.16975 2.25331C9.17539 1.57852 11.3796 2.58838 12.1639 4.5795L13.1718 7.13811C13.273 7.39504 13.1465 7.68534 12.8895 7.78655C12.6327 7.88749 12.3423 7.76113 12.2411 7.50432L11.2333 4.94571C10.6259 3.40439 8.88406 2.6471 7.3426 3.25429C5.80118 3.86161 5.04399 5.60345 5.65118 7.14494L6.659 9.70355C6.76021 9.96048 6.6337 10.2508 6.37677 10.352C6.11988 10.4531 5.82952 10.3266 5.72833 10.0698L4.7205 7.51116C3.91111 5.45581 4.92107 3.13323 6.97639 2.32362L7.16975 2.25331Z" /></svg></span>Blog</span></span></a></div></div></div></div></section><section id="faqAccordion" data-section="faqAccordion" data-cta-section="faqAccordion" class="SectionWrapper-module-scss-module__NFbz_a__wrapper theme-main"><div class="SectionWrapper-module-scss-module__NFbz_a__borderTop"></div><div class="container"><div class="IntroBlock-module-scss-module__0mSC7a__introBlock IntroBlock-module-scss-module__0mSC7a__spacingBelowLarge" style="--intro-headline-width:30ch"><div class="Illustration-module-scss-module__pBGuRG__base Illustration-module-scss-module__pBGuRG__pictogram Illustration-module-scss-module__pBGuRG__size-large IntroBlock-module-scss-module__0mSC7a__pictogram" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a question mark symbol with a dot below, rendered in beige and dark brown colors on a transparent background"></div><h2 class="Heading-module-scss-module__AyGdUq__heading text-headline-1-serif Heading-module-scss-module__AyGdUq__balance AnimatedHeading-module-scss-module__KoWePa__heading IntroBlock-module-scss-module__0mSC7a__headline IntroBlock-module-scss-module__0mSC7a__headlineBalance" style="--word-stagger:0s" aria-label="FAQ"><span class="AnimatedHeading-module-scss-module__KoWePa__word" style="--word-index:0" aria-hidden="true">FAQ</span></h2></div><div class="AsideRails-module-scss-module__sFf8jW__root" data-measure="narrow"><div class="AsideRails-module-scss-module__sFf8jW__content AsideRails-module-scss-module__sFf8jW__contentNarrow"><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__accordion FAQAccordionLayout-module-scss-module__R1kBVG__column"><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__item"><h3><button type="button" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-e5d063f95b69-a67e6168d71d" data-cta-ignore=""><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__question text-headline-6-serif">Where is this available?</span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__icon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBar"></span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBarVertical"></span></span></button></h3><div id="faq-e5d063f95b69-a67e6168d71d" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__content" inert=""><div class="text-rich-text FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__body"><p class="text-body-2">Admins can enable Claude Security in the <a href="http://claude.ai/admin-settings/claude-code">admin console</a>. See the getting started guide for <a href="https://academy.claude.com/tutorials/getting-started-with-claude-security">setup steps</a>.</p><p class="text-body-2">The <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/claude-security">Claude Security plugin</a> is now available in beta for all Claude Code users.</p></div></div></div><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__item"><h3><button type="button" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-e5d063f95b69-83e943a0f59d" data-cta-ignore=""><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__question text-headline-6-serif">What Mythos access does this give me?</span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__icon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBar"></span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBarVertical"></span></span></button></h3><div id="faq-e5d063f95b69-83e943a0f59d" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__content" inert=""><div class="text-rich-text FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__body"><p class="text-body-2">Claude Security is powered by our full family of models, including Claude Mythos, with no Cyber Verification Program access required. </p><p class="text-body-2">Create a project, connect your repositories, and Claude Security scans them using our most capable models for cyber, including Claude Mythos models. Validated findings come back with severity ratings and suggested fixes, which you can open in Claude Code and fix using the models available in your account. </p><p class="text-body-2"><em>Scans powered by Claude Mythos models are only available in the Claude Security app on Claude.ai. The Claude Security plugin for Claude Code uses the models available in your Claude Code account.</em></p></div></div></div><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__item"><h3><button type="button" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-e5d063f95b69-3b947787db28" data-cta-ignore=""><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__question text-headline-6-serif">What are the security risks I should know about?</span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__icon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBar"></span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBarVertical"></span></span></button></h3><div id="faq-e5d063f95b69-3b947787db28" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__content" inert=""><div class="text-rich-text FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__body"><p class="text-body-2">Claude can make mistakes, so you should always review proposed patches before applying them, especially for critical systems.</p></div></div></div><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__item"><h3><button type="button" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-e5d063f95b69-2dea4c4cc7a9" data-cta-ignore=""><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__question text-headline-6-serif">What types of vulnerabilities does Claude Security find?</span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__icon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBar"></span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBarVertical"></span></span></button></h3><div id="faq-e5d063f95b69-2dea4c4cc7a9" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__content" inert=""><div class="text-rich-text FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__body"><p class="text-body-2">Claude Security focuses on high-severity vulnerabilities including memory corruption, injection flaws, authentication bypasses, and complex logic errors that pattern-matching tools typically miss. It&#x27;s particularly effective at finding context-dependent vulnerabilities that require understanding code across multiple files.</p></div></div></div><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__item"><h3><button type="button" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-e5d063f95b69-7520a92feeef" data-cta-ignore=""><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__question text-headline-6-serif">How is this different from traditional security tools?</span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__icon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBar"></span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBarVertical"></span></span></button></h3><div id="faq-e5d063f95b69-7520a92feeef" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__content" inert=""><div class="text-rich-text FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__body"><p class="text-body-2">Traditional tools often use rule-based pattern matching, which catches known vulnerability patterns but can produce high false positive rates and miss complex issues. Claude Security reasons through your code like a security researcher. It can read Git history, trace data flows, and understand business logic to find real vulnerabilities and generate real fixes.</p></div></div></div><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__item"><h3><button type="button" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-e5d063f95b69-1bd0c8bc8480" data-cta-ignore=""><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__question text-headline-6-serif">Does Claude Security work with my existing security tools?</span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__icon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBar"></span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBarVertical"></span></span></button></h3><div id="faq-e5d063f95b69-1bd0c8bc8480" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__content" inert=""><div class="text-rich-text FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__body"><p class="text-body-2">Yes. The Claude Security API lets you pull findings into your ticketing, vulnerability management, and reporting tools. You can also resolve or reopen them from there. Webhooks notify your systems when you receive a new finding.</p><p class="text-body-2">Claude Security is also available as an MCP connector in Claude and Claude Code, so an engineer can pull up a finding, start the fix, and mark it resolved in the same session.</p></div></div></div><div class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__item"><h3><button type="button" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__trigger" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-e5d063f95b69-87fbbca16f49" data-cta-ignore=""><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__question text-headline-6-serif">Do I need to schedule scans?</span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__icon" aria-hidden="true"><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBar"></span><span class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__iconBarVertical"></span></span></button></h3><div id="faq-e5d063f95b69-87fbbca16f49" class="FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__content" inert=""><div class="text-rich-text FAQAccordion-module-scss-module__nWoFyW__body"><p class="text-body-2">No. Choose the branch and scope for each repository, and Claude runs a deep baseline scan. After that it keeps scanning changes regularly based on their risk and complexity, so your findings stay close to the current state of your code.</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Where is this available?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Admins can enable Claude Security in the admin console. See the getting started guide for setup steps.\n\nThe Claude Security plugin is now available in beta for all Claude Code users."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Mythos access does this give me?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Security is powered by our full family of models, including Claude Mythos, with no Cyber Verification Program access required. \n\nCreate a project, connect your repositories, and Claude Security scans them using our most capable models for cyber, including Claude Mythos models. Validated findings come back with severity ratings and suggested fixes, which you can open in Claude Code and fix using the models available in your account. \n\nScans powered by Claude Mythos models are only available in the Claude Security app on Claude.ai. The Claude Security plugin for Claude Code uses the models available in your Claude Code account."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the security risks I should know about?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude can make mistakes, so you should always review proposed patches before applying them, especially for critical systems."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of vulnerabilities does Claude Security find?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Claude Security focuses on high-severity vulnerabilities including memory corruption, injection flaws, authentication bypasses, and complex logic errors that pattern-matching tools typically miss. It's particularly effective at finding context-dependent vulnerabilities that require understanding code across multiple files."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How is this different from traditional security tools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Traditional tools often use rule-based pattern matching, which catches known vulnerability patterns but can produce high false positive rates and miss complex issues. Claude Security reasons through your code like a security researcher. It can read Git history, trace data flows, and understand business logic to find real vulnerabilities and generate real fixes."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Claude Security work with my existing security tools?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Claude Security API lets you pull findings into your ticketing, vulnerability management, and reporting tools. You can also resolve or reopen them from there. Webhooks notify your systems when you receive a new finding.\n\nClaude Security is also available as an MCP connector in Claude and Claude Code, so an engineer can pull up a finding, start the fix, and mark it resolved in the same session."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need to schedule scans?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Choose the branch and scope for each repository, and Claude runs a deep baseline scan. After that it keeps scanning changes regularly based on their risk and complexity, so your findings stay close to the current state of your code."}}]}</script></div></main></div><footer class="Footer-module-scss-module__fZonEa__footer theme-dark" data-cta-section="footer"><div class="container"><div class="Footer-module-scss-module__fZonEa__grid"><div class="Footer-module-scss-module__fZonEa__logoColumn"><div><a href="/" class="Footer-module-scss-module__fZonEa__logo"><svg class="ClaudeWordmark-module-scss-module__u-w1aa__claudeWordmark" viewBox="0 0 573 125" fill="currentColor" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-label="Claude"><path d="M200.168 110.625C190.376 110.625 181.647 108.688 173.98 104.813C166.355 100.896 160.397 95.4167 156.105 88.375C151.814 81.3333 149.668 73.25 149.668 64.125C149.668 54.4167 151.855 45.7917 156.23 38.25C160.647 30.7083 166.751 24.8542 174.543 20.6875C182.335 16.4792 191.189 14.375 201.105 14.375C207.064 14.375 213.001 15.0208 218.918 16.3125C224.876 17.5625 230.105 19.5208 234.605 22.1875V42.75H228.98C227.397 35.2083 224.293 29.7292 219.668 26.3125C215.085 22.8958 208.814 21.1875 200.855 21.1875C193.23 21.1875 186.897 22.8958 181.855 26.3125C176.814 29.7292 173.085 34.5 170.668 40.625C168.251 46.7083 167.043 53.7917 167.043 61.875C167.043 69.8333 168.397 76.9792 171.105 83.3125C173.814 89.6458 177.835 94.6458 183.168 98.3125C188.501 101.979 194.918 103.813 202.418 103.813C207.501 103.813 211.855 102.813 215.48 100.813C219.147 98.8125 222.23 96.0833