mes\":null,\"still\":null,\"alt\":\"Illustration of a question mark symbol with a dot below, rendered in beige and dark brown colors on a transparent background\",\"className\":\"IntroBlock-module-scss-module__0mSC7a__pictogram\",\"size\":\"large\"}],null,null,\"$L4d\",null]}],\"$L4e\"],null]}],\"$undefined\"]}]\n4f:Tc79,{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"FAQPage\",\"mainEntity\":[{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Where is this available?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Admins can enable Claude Security in the admin console. See the getting started guide for setup steps.\\n\\nThe Claude Security plugin is now available in beta for all Claude Code users.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What Mythos access does this give me?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Claude Security is powered by our full family of models, including Claude Mythos, with no Cyber Verification Program access required. \\n\\nCreate a project, connect your repositories, and Claude Security scans them using our most capable models for cyber, including Claude Mythos models. Validated findings come back with severity ratings and suggested fixes, which you can open in Claude Code and fix using the models available in your account. \\n\\nScans powered by Claude Mythos models are only available in the Claude Security app on Claude.ai. The Claude Security plugin for Claude Code uses the models available in your Claude Code account.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What are the security risks I should know about?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Claude can make mistakes, so you should always review proposed patches before applying them, especially for critical systems.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What types of vulnerabilities does Claude Security find?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Claude Security focuses on high-severity vulnerabilities including memory corruption, injection flaws, authentication bypasses, and complex logic errors that pattern-matching tools typically miss. It's particularly effective at finding context-dependent vulnerabilities that require understanding code across multiple files.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How is this different from traditional security tools?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Traditional tools often use rule-based pattern matching, which catches known vulnerability patterns but can produce high false positive rates and miss complex issues. Claude Security reasons through your code like a security researcher. It can read Git history, trace data"])</script><script nonce="ra8XbZYlV5PcbbCdB45pwg==">self.__next_f.push([1," flows, and understand business logic to find real vulnerabilities and generate real fixes.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does Claude Security work with my existing security tools?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. The Claude Security API lets you pull findings into your ticketing, vulnerability management, and reporting tools. You can also resolve or reopen them from there. Webhooks notify your systems when you receive a new finding.\\n\\nClaude Security is also available as an MCP connector in Claude and Claude Code, so an engineer can pull up a finding, start the fix, and mark it resolved in the same session.\"}},{\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do I need to schedule scans?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"No. Choose the branch and scope for each repository, and Claude runs a deep baseline scan. After that it keeps scanning changes regularly based on their risk and complexity, so your findings stay close to the current state of your code.\"}}]}3b:[\"$\",\"script\",\"faq-json-ld\",{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$4f\"}}]\n50:I[614751,[\"/_next/static/chunks/14f50671ce8aedb8.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/2cb2d97b398e993a.js\",\"/_next/static/chunks/00de5bce2a50b9b